<article class="env-lemma" id="05N6">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05N6">Lemma <span data-tag="05N6">8.7.5.20</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [rr]^-{F} \ar [dr]_{U} &amp;  &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' \ar [dl]^{ U' } \\ &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, &amp;  } \]
</div>
<p> where $U$ is a flat inner fibration, $U'$ is an inner fibration, and $F$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. Then: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the induced map of fibers $F_{C}: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'_{C}$ is a Morita equivalence. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The inner fibration $U'$ is flat. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof of Lemma <a data-tag="05N6" href="/tag/05N6">8.7.5.20</a>.</strong>
       We will prove $(1)$; assertion $(2)$ then follows from Example <a data-tag="05MW" href="/tag/05MW">8.7.5.10</a>. Using Corollary <a data-tag="02VM" href="/tag/02VM">4.5.3.24</a>, we can factor $U'$ as a composition $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' \xrightarrow {G} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'' \xrightarrow {U''} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, where $U''$ is an isofibration and $G$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. For each object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the map of fibers $G_{C}: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'_{C} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}''_{C}$ is fully faithful (Proposition <a data-tag="05P5" href="/tag/05P5">4.8.3.7</a>). Consequently, to show that $F_{C}$ is a Morita equivalence, it will suffice to show that $G_{C} \circ F_{C}$ is a Morita equivalence (see Proposition <a data-tag="05MG" href="/tag/05MG">8.5.6.11</a>). We may therefore replace $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$ by $calE''$ are thereby reduce to proving assertion $(1)$ under the additional assumption that $U'$ is an isofibration. 
    <p>
      Using Corollary <a data-tag="02VM" href="/tag/02VM">4.5.3.24</a>, we can factor the inclusion map $\{ C\}  \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ as a composition $\{ C\}  \hookrightarrow \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \xrightarrow {V} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, where $V$ is an isofibration and $\widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ is a contractible Kan complex. Set $\widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} = \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ and $\widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}' = \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$, so that we have a commutative diagram of $\infty $-categories 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C} \ar [r]^-{F_{C}} \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'_{C} \ar [d] \\ \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} \ar [r]^-{\widetilde{F}} &amp;  \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}'. } \]
</div>
<p>
       It follows from Theorem <a data-tag="05MS" href="/tag/05MS">8.7.5.6</a> that the left vertical map is a Morita equivalence, and from Corollary <a data-tag="01HJ" href="/tag/01HJ">4.5.3.33</a> that the right vertical and bottom horizontal maps are equivalences of $\infty $-categories. Applying Remark <a data-tag="05MD" href="/tag/05MD">8.5.6.6</a>, we conclude that $F_{C}$ is also a Morita equivalence. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
